# ---------------------------------
#   Debian applications Discover never offers to build in a box.
#
# One Debian package name a line. Each is a desktop application of Debian's
# DEP-11 catalogue that cannot do its job from a box on KWin's Wayland
# session, so a build of it would install something that does not work.
# The Debian lane leaves each out of every search, category and appstream://
# link; a box already made for one is still listed, so it can be removed.
# A catalogue row naming one of these packages is not affected. The image
# build turns this list into /usr/share/swcatalog/xml/kdos-debian-exclude.xml,
# which takes each application out of every AppStream pool on the machine,
# so KRunner's software results do not offer one either; an application
# whose id a host port also has keeps its component there.
# ---------------------------------

# Work only on an X server's own screen: a box reaches the session through
# Xwayland, where a magnifier sees no Wayland window, a pointer tool moves
# no pointer and an on-screen keyboard types into no other application.
eviacam
gxneur
kmag
kmousetool
onboard
spotlighter

# Plug-ins and settings of other compositors and shells.
compiz-core
compizconfig-settings-manager
gnome-shell-extension-manager
gnome-shell-extension-prefs
gnome-tweaks
wstroke

# Read the systemd journal, which KDOS does not have.
gnome-logs

# Manage a Debian system's own packages, which a box is not.
gnome-software
plasma-discover
synaptic

# Configure a firewall daemon the host does not run (firewalld, ufw,
# opensnitchd); the host's packet filter is kdos-powerd's nftables ruleset,
# set from System Settings' Firewall page.
firewall-config
gufw
python3-opensnitch-ui

# Need the host's disks.
gnome-disk-utility
gparted
timeshift
